  led him to turn away from the spotlight  isaac hempstead wright landed the role  of bran stark  in game of thrones at just 12 years old  his prior on-screen experience was a  small part in the horror movie  the awakening that had yet to be  released as bran  he arguably instigated a large portion  of the plot of the entire show  since his discovery of jamie and cersei  lannister's incestuous affair  this led to his serious fall thanks to  jaime which was the inciting incident  of the pilot the things i do for love  bran would go on to weave one of the  most unique journeys through westeros  over the course of the show paralyzed  from the waist down  he learns to adapt to his new life just  in time to escape to the north when  winterfell is captured by theon greyjoy  he then hones his ability to warg into  his dire wolf  and is eventually trained by a mystical  man known as the three-eyed raven  in the art of green sight which  essentially means having visions of the  past  this enables him to discern the game of  thrones twist that most of the audience  saw coming from a mile away  that is jon snow's true parentage as an  heir to the iron throne in a shocking  turn that even hempstead wright thought  was a joke at first  bran ends up on the throne at the  story's end he also winds up with a  mouthful of a title  as tyrion says in full bran the broken  the first of his name  king of the andals and the first men  lord of the six kingdoms and protector  of the realm isaac hempstead wright  meanwhile was struggling to find  normalcy behind the scenes while his  alter ego took such strange turns  on a huge hit tv show he told esquire uk  that game of thrones all but ruined his  college experience he shared  my address got published i couldn't walk  out of my halls without having to take a  selfie  eventually i got assigned a campus  police officer  he dropped out but eventually returned  to university college london to study  neuroscience  focusing on his studies he naturally  took a break from acting until appearing  in a minor role  in the 2021 film voyagers in april  of 2021. jacob anderson gained  prominence with recurring roles on  broadchurch and episodes before landing  the role of grey worm  as the elected leader of the unsullied a  group of eunuch warriors raised his  slaves  he displays a fierce devotion to  daenerys targaryen for freeing him  and all of his brethren he chooses to  fight for her as one of her most trusted  lieutenants  eventually he has time amidst all the  late season chaos for a doomed romance  with daenerys advisor  missandei in sales with the remaining  unsullied missandei's homeland  at the end of the series anderson didn't  do much other acting during his time on  game of thrones  and hasn't appeared on screen since the  series ended but don't worry that  casting directors are giving this  talented actor the cold shoulder  he stepped out of the film and  television spotlight because he's  focusing on his music career  as a pop and r b singer known as raleigh  richie  few characters during all of game of  thrones were more compelling  and few deaths more heart-wrenching than  shireen baratheon  the only surviving child of stannis  baratheon she's treated coldly by her  father as he pursues the iron throne  after his brother's death  she doesn't get any more warmth from her  mother who resents her for being  partially disfigured from a disease  known as grayscale she finds comfort  however in her friendship with the kind  sir davos  who is in her father's service shireen  even demonstrates ingenuity at multiple  points that aids her father in his  various battles and quests  across the series ultimately however  he's convinced by the sorceress  melisandre  during a desperate moment that a  sacrifice of king's blood  will help turn the tide in his favor and  shireen is his only option  in a scene that many fans found  unnecessarily cruel poor shireen is  burned alive as her mother cries in  anguish and stannis looks away in tears  this show  really could get pretty dark when it  wanted to the english actress carrie  ingram brought shereen to life and  unlike her on-screen counterpart she  remains thankfully alive and well  already the winner of an olivier award  for starring in matilda the musical  before game of thrones  she made a few other tv appearances she  was actually a series regular  on free reign during the run of thrones  but hasn't had any appearances since it  ended  in 2019 the pandemic likely played a  role  but we'll surely be hearing from carrie  ingram in the future  luke barnes is primarily a british  playwright and screenwriter with only a  single acting role as drunk man  in an episode of skins to his name  before playing rast on game of thrones  nevertheless he left an indelible mark  as one of several unsavory villains that  jon snow encounters during his time at  castle black with a nice watch  rast is a foul criminal that took the  black and pledged service  the night's watch instead of a worse  punishment he torments jon's friend sam  during training and acts clearly envious  of jon's skill  an increasingly prominent role as the  months pass  he stabs the honorable lord commander  mormont in the back  during the mutiny at craster's keep and  later even tortures  poor hodor when the mutineers briefly  detain him  along with bran stark his eventual death  at the pause of jon snow's direwolf  ghost is one of several very satisfying  ones  over the course of this extremely  death-friendly show  after wrapping his time on game of  thrones barnes did have a couple small  parts in short films  but hasn't appeared on screen since the  show ended instead he's returned to his  native northern ireland to focus on  writing and producing theater once more  like many of the other child actors on  game of thrones ben hockey had just a  few small roles  before appearing as hot pie friend of  arya stark  an orphan who's been sent to the night's  watch 